From 294f440a8a45c4fdb76d8ec814b537844bd3492c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:29:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/28] (b) v2, part b-3: \caption* label removes the usual
 separators

The label that \caption* passes to \@makecaption, \@caption@nolabel,
removed only a colon directly after it. Reviews of round 1 found
(findings F1, F3, N1, F5):

- adfathesis.cls and every \@makecaption of the form {#1: }\vadjust..
  stopped with "You can't use \vadjust in internal vertical mode": with
  the colon removed nothing started the paragraph (regression).
- {\bfseries #1:} #2 (ntgclass, paper.cls), #1:~#2, \textbf{#1}: #2
  and the many classes with a period (llncs {\bfseries #1.} #2,
  IEEEtran, mwcls #1.\enspace#2, toptesi, ...) kept a leading space or
  their separator; toptesi's test for an empty label gave ". Text".
- Classes whose separator is in a macro (KOMA-Script, memoir, amsart,
  babel-french with pdfTeX) printed it silently.

The contract for \@makecaption is unchanged and now stated in one place:
\if@captionstar is true and the label is \@caption@nolabel (never
empty); a \@makecaption that supports \caption* tests the switch, which
is the only documented test. For definitions that do not, the label
removes the usual separators after it: a colon or a period, then
spaces, ~, \nobreakspace, \space, \ , \enspace, \enskip, \quad or
\qquad, also after the end of a group or of \textbf and the other text
font commands (\check@icr; their \maybe@ic after the group is dropped).
If something is removed, a paragraph is started, as the removed
material would have done. Nothing of the text is removed, since it
starts with \ignorespaces. If another command follows the label
directly (a separator macro, \hskip), it is printed and a warning is
given once per document. The label only does this while
\if@captionstar is true.

Class sweep (pdfLaTeX, 107 TL classes of which 22 do not compile with
pdfLaTeX at all, \caption* short and long,
compared with the previous head): 23 classes now give the text alone
(adfathesis without its error, llncs, mwart/mwrep/mwbk, ntgclass,
paper, spie, toptesi, ltugboat, aiaa-tc, amsldoc, ua-thesis, uafthesis,
ucdavisthesis, stb-thesis, usthesis); 21 still print a separator or
space and now warn (amsart/amsbook/amsproc, KOMA-Script, memoir,
revtex4-1/4-2, bxjs*, jpsj2, ptptex, disser, ...); no new errors. With
\DocumentMetadata the tagging \@makecaption is used and all are clean.

Documentation: ltfloat.dtx (contract, the label), clsguide (only the
switch is a test; a separator macro is printed; code that replaces
\caption passes \@caption@nolabel, not an empty label), usrguide
(separators of KOMA-Script, memoir, AMS classes, babel-french).

Test: caption-interface-001 test 26 with the label in 19 forms of
\@makecaption, the warning and a \vadjust after {#1: }.
